hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1086","Chapter on not seeking the aid of the polytheists, 1124 - Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tarsusi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): A man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was heading for Badr: Shall I go out with you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not seek the aid of a polytheist."
